1871 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Modeling the impacts of precipitation on sanitary sewer flow is challenging due to limited\055duration flow metering records\054 complex interactions among static and time\055varying factors\054 and short\055term\054 long\055term\054 and seasonal hydrologic processes\056 The traditional calibration approach adjusts and optimizes parameters for all processes simultaneously to attempt to match the measured flow rate\056\nIn this study\054 we present an alternative calibration approach that first disaggregates the measured sewer flow signal into four sub\055signals\054 each of which represents a different hydrologic process\056 Then each hydrologic process is independently modeled and calibrated\240 to its own distinct sub\055signal\056 This approach significantly reduces the parameter solution domain\054 resulting in faster\054 and more reliable and confident calibration\056)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 1872 0 R
     /Pg 1864 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1872 0 obj
  << /K [ 6 1871 0 R ]
     /P 2013 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1864 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

